uture it's more  about what you believe the fortune means  disheartened Sage left the restaurant  his head hanging low as he walked down  the street towards the sidewalk he felt  his phone vibrate in this pocket taking  a look at the screen still walking he  saw a text from Joey he was asking if  Sage had any luck asking the restaurant  about his fortune cookie maybe if Sage  had done with a fateful slip of paper  I'd told him as he stepped off the  sidewalk then he would have seen the bus  speeding down the road towards him if  you want to know the future perhaps you  should only look at your own risk  sometimes knowing exactly what is  destined to happen to you can make it  impossible to avoid a self-fulfilling  prophecy if you will that is the warning  given to any who dares to take a  prediction from  scp-377 now residing in the personal  break room at one of the SCP  foundation's sites  scp-377 is the designation given to an  anomalous box of fortune cookies the  fact that the box is seemingly capable  of Replay punishing itself at regular  intervals refilling every 12 hours  happens to be the far less interesting  thing about it any of the fortune  cookies taken from  scp-377r well the cookies themselves are  completely Ordinary by any and all  metrics they taste exactly as fortune  cookies should and they aren't made of  any ingredients apart from those you'd  expect but somehow without fail every  single Fortune found within one of these  crispy confectionary Clairvoyance  manages to be 100 accurate they aren't  generalized predictions for the future  definitely none of them have prophesized  who the next winners of the World Series  are going to be or who is next in line  to be president every Fortune contained  in the scp-377 cookies are specifically  tailored to the person who opens them  these fortunes have ranged from detailed  foreknowledge of upcoming events and  changes in someone's personal life to  vague unspecified Illusions to what lies  ahead and while always factually  accurate and perfectly aligned with the  future the predictions made by these  cookies are not always Promises of Good  Fortune One researcher opened up an  scp-377 fortune cookie only to read the  phrase It's a boy written on the paper  less than an hour later his wife's water  broke and said researcher was soon  welcoming his newborn baby son into the  world but another doctor was warned you  don't have long to live right before  choking on his own cookie right there in  the break room that doctor suffocated  killed by the same thing that foretold  of his death only moments before it is  for that reason that SCP Foundation  Personnel are given a warning before  helping themselves to a sugary shelled  treat all staff are permitted to open a  cookie from scp-377 after all they are  safe to eat and Foundation employees are  also welcome to read their fortunes  however they only do so at their own  risk now go and check out scp-261  pan-dimensional vending machine and  scp-348 a gift from Dad if you're still  feeling for more appetizing anomalies  and snack-worthy scps to satiate your  hunger
 

